\title{mapSpainHist: Historical Municipal Boundaries of Spain (1900-2001)}
\description{
Municipal boundaries for each population census between 1900 and 2001, plus
provinces, judicial districts and electoral districts built from them. All maps
derive from a single partition of the territory, so they have no gaps or
overlaps and aggregate consistently.
}
\section{Warning}{
 approximate boundaries:
For most historical municipalities there is no cartography of their limits.
Their polygons were reconstructed approximately from the earliest available
official municipal division (early 2000s), making sure that the municipal seat
(the settlement that usually names the municipality) and, when known, the other
settlements of the municipality fall inside the polygon. The maps are especially
useful to represent municipal data graphically, but they must be used with
caution when geographic variables matter (area, distances, exact borders): they
are a useful but imperfect approximation.
}

